            <p>Pulmonary Artery and Vein Distribution in a Primary Lobule. This schematic longitudinal section illustrates the branching of the pulmonary artery (red) and pulmonary vein (blue) within a primary lobule of the lung. Pulmonary arteries follow the bronchioles and supply alveolar capillaries, while pulmonary veins run independently through interlobular septa and drain oxygenated blood into larger tributaries. Henry Vandyke Carter, <ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?search=Gray+plate+975&#x00026;title=Special:MediaSearch&#x00026;go=Go&#x00026;type=image">Public Domain</ext-link>, via Wikimedia Commons</p>
